From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve PON session during WLAN station cleanup

Keep a valid exclusive production PON session across unrelated WLAN WCID
revocation. The WLAN flush caller still advances the station epoch and
removes stale flow rows. Preserve fail-close on epoch exhaustion and the
existing owner notification for global, LAN1 and inactive-session revokes.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ct_native_pair.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ct_native_pair.h
@@ -348,6 +348,12 @@
 	int err;
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&ppe_lock);
+	/* WLAN teardown keeps the exclusive PON session; the caller retires
+	 * the station epoch and stale WLAN flow rows. */
+	if (band >= 0 && band <= 1 && wcid && wcid <= 150 &&
+	    airoha_ppe_npu_production_active(ppe, ppe->ct_npu_owner))
+		return ppe->ct_wlan_epoch[band][wcid] == U32_MAX ?
+			airoha_ct_pair_fail(ppe, -EOVERFLOW) : 0;
 	if (ppe->ct_host_ppe) {
 		err = airoha_npu_owner_notify(ppe, NULL);
 		if (err)
